Fine. On fremont:

```bash
cd ~
git clone https://gitcode.com/TritonAscendTest/Q3TritonKernel.git
cd Q3TritonKernel
ls
```

It may prompt for `yaolu0211` and your access token.

Then copy to the A5:

```bash
scp -r ~/Q3TritonKernel root@141.61.33.141:/home/yaolu/
```

Fremont can already reach the A5 on port 22, so this should go through. It may ask for the root password.

Then on the A5:

```bash
source /home/yaolu/env.sh
cd /home/yaolu/Q3TritonKernel
ls
cat requirements.txt 2>/dev/null
pytest -s tests/fla_perf/test_nsa_compression_kernels_perf.py::test_nsa_compression_fwd_kernel_perf
```

Note you don't need to be inside the a5-ubuntu container on fremont for the clone. Do it from the plain fremont shell, since the container shares your home anyway.
